// Refusal fixture: a WHILE loop whose trip count depends on a varying.
//
// The general path lowers a run-time-bound `for` to a hardware loop
// (LOOP / BRK, FP-LOOP slice 1) but not a `while`: that keeps the CFG
// back-edge, which the flatten refuses (CF-1a).  The fixture pins the
// refusal CONTRACT (nonzero exit, no container, a printed refusal) on a
// shape that still refuses; when `while` loops are lowered it has to move
// to another still-refused shape.  It used to be the `for` form of this
// loop, which now compiles (tests/shader-compiler/fp-hardware-loop-test.sh).
//
// Used by tests/shader-compiler/refusal-semantics-test.sh, which
// asserts the full refusal, not just the diagnostic: nonzero exit AND
// no container file.  Shipped v0.12.21's general path printed
// "unsupported IR op" and then wrote a container and exited 0 - a
// plausible artifact where there should have been a refusal; this test
// exists so that hole cannot silently reopen.

void main(
    float4 in_texcoord   : TEXCOORD0,
    out float4 out_color : COLOR)
{
    float acc = 0.0f;
    int n = (int)(in_texcoord.x * 10.0f);
    int i = 0;
    while (i < n) {
        acc = acc + 0.1f;
        i++;
    }
    out_color = float4(acc, 0.0f, 0.0f, 1.0f);
}
